[[Eathon Lambert]] found the puzzle, but was unable to use it because he never made it to [[Atlantis]], so he left it in a secret room in the [[Tomb of Nefertiti]] instead. He drew on the wall a code to find it that only his son, [[Lok Lambert|Lok]], would be able to solve. {{source|The Sceptre Deception}}

Lok discovered it whilst revealing to [[Cherit]] in the [[Tomb of Nefertiti]] that [[Sandra Lambert]] had got him a bird when he was six, contrary to the bicycle, baseball bat and toy he had wanted. {{source|The Sceptre Deception}}

